{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 45, :comments ["<b>צפנת פענח.</b> Revealer of hidden things, and it has no parallel in Scripture, but we find it in the יוצר prayer: 'המפענח נעלמים' — who unravels mysteries. According to this, the king knew the language of the land of Canaan, which was near him; and likewise Bityah his daughter gave him a name in the holy tongue — for Moses our master — on account of 'כי מן המים משיתיהו.'" "<b>בת פוטי פרע כהן און.</b> Our Rabbis, of blessed memory, interpreted: Potiphera is Potiphar. He was called Potiphar because he fattened (מפטם) bulls and calves for idolatry, and this is the meaning of Potiphar — מפטם פר. He was called Potiphar, and he was called Potiphera because he was castrated (נסתרס) on his account, because he took Joseph for the lying of a male." "<b>And my opinion</b> is to say that Potiphera was one of Pharaoh's chief officers, and when he was castrated and they changed his name to Potiphera, he was ashamed of the matter and became a priest in a house of idolatry, and this is what is written of him: כהן און — the god of On was his god; and likewise we find with Jethro, of whom it is written כהן מדין, and its meaning is priest, because he fattened calves for idolatry. And they said in the Midrash that Osnat was Dinah's daughter, and she was from Shechem son of Hamor; and because Jacob drove her from his house and placed her among a certain thornbush (סנה), therefore she was called Osnat. What did Jacob do? He tied a writ around her neck, and written on it was: 'all who cleave to you cleaves to the seed of Jacob.' And Joseph, when he married her, saw that writ and kept it hidden, and this is what he said to his father (Genesis 48): 'בני הם אשר נתן לי אלהים בזה' — with this he showed him that writ." "And what is written, <b>בת פוטיפרע</b> [the daughter of Potiphera], is because she was raised in his house — for thus our Rabbis, of blessed memory, interpreted: whoever raises an orphan in his house, Scripture accounts it to him as though he begot the child."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 41, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:19:41.270360585Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}